{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And the sense of <b>to lie beside her</b> is according to the words of Rabbi Abraham — even if he were to lie beside her in proximity, she in her garment and he in his garment, or to be with her to converse, for we do not find \"אֶצְלָהּ\" (beside her) used for intercourse, but only \"with her\" or \"her\": \"lie with me,\" \"if a man lies with her\" (Leviticus 15:24), \"and the women shall be lain with\" (Zechariah 14:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "\"Rabbi Abraham\" refers to Ibn Ezra, whom Ramban frequently cites by this epithet."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:59.257333227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}